    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "55c58a5b_75a008ac",
        "filename": "Makefile.rules",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001139
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-10-30T17:57:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"all\" is already defined in Makefile. How about this:\n\nIn Makefile, change \"all\" to:\n\n  all: $(out)/$(PROJECT).bin utils spi_image\n\nand here, do something like:\n\n  ifeq \"$(PACK_SPI_IMAGE)\" \"y\"\n  spi_image: $(out)/$(PROJECT).spi.bin\n  else\n  spi_image:\n  endif\n\nand in board/strago/build.mk:\n\n  PACK_SPI_IMAGE:\u003dy",
      "revId": "0be80ce96799257ecf138c458c5316d4abfda564",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "15bf92c3_968e8a89",
        "filename": "Makefile.rules",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1110034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-10-30T21:31:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"all is already defined\"\nMake has always allowed additional prerequisites to be added to a target. If it didn\u0027t then all the various automatic and manual dependency management scripts wouldn\u0027t work.\n  \n\n\"make spi_image a new phony target and have a 5 line ifeq-else-endif to make it depend on something\"\n\nOne could make such a change. I think it goes against the spirit of the existing makefile structure. The typical use of \"ifeq\" in a \"Dancing Makefiles\" setup is to set up a series of variables. Then the variables are used elsewhere.\n\nI don\u0027t see any advantage in your proposal. The 5 line ifeq...endif could be written as the 1 line in Makefile\nspi_image: $(PACK_SPI_IMAGE)\nand in board/strago/build.mk\nPACK_SPI_IMAGE\u003d $(out)/$(PROJECT).spi.bin\n\n(obviously add spi_image to the .PHONY as well). This just adds another indirection. Perhaps change the name of spi-y to PROJECT_EXTRAS?",
      "parentUuid": "55c58a5b_75a008ac",
      "revId": "0be80ce96799257ecf138c458c5316d4abfda564",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "15f87289_f4afceee",
        "filename": "Makefile.rules",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001139
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-10-30T21:45:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m sure it works, but defining \"all\" in 2 places makes it more difficult to figure out what happens when you do \"make all\".\n\nThe reason that I prefer not to put the output file name in board/strago/build.mk is that we\u0027ll have other board/chip that need SPI image, and the file name of the SPI image should be the same. Therefore, putting the file name there would just force us to copy-and-paste in the future. As for the 5-line ifeq, yes, you can do without it by:\n\n  SPI_IMAGE-$(PACK_SPI_IMAGE)\u003d$(out)/$(PROJECT).spi.bin\n  spi_image: $(SPI_IMAGE-y)",
      "parentUuid": "15bf92c3_968e8a89",
      "revId": "0be80ce96799257ecf138c458c5316d4abfda564",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
